r government as  part of the German surrender Germany  reduced its military to 100 000  individuals and disbanded its Air Force  altogether  after some vigorous political arm  twisting and the odd persuasive nipple  [ __ ] thrown in for good measure  Germany also accepted full  responsibility for the war and agreed to  pay billions of dollars in reparations  to the rest of Europe  that was all very good in principle but  in practice Germany was practically  penniless and so the Weimar government  came up with a genius economic plan to  pay off its mounting debts it started  printing money by the truckload yeah you  don't need to have an economics degree  to see where this one's going all that  shiny new money flooded the German  economy triggering Mass hyperinflation  that at its worst saw 4.2 trillion  German marks being worth a single US  dollar  if you were unfortunate enough to be a  German citizen in the early 1920s  you didn't keep your money in a wallet  you needed a wheelbarrow like literally  people actually did that  by 1924 the German economy was on the  floor industrial output was at an  all-time low and widespread food  shortages left Millions on the point of  starvation  but just when the fields were fully  fallow help came from an unlikely fellow  the United States a country with which  Germany had been at War just six years  before  under what became known as the doors  plan Germany borrowed huge sums of money  from American Banks to fund a booming  cultural and economic recovery in the  mid to late 1920s  now running your country on farming  credit might sound a bit risky but the  Weimar government wasn't worried that  they were borrowing from America the  wealthiest most stable country in the  world what could possibly go wrong  as it happens that question had a free  Word answer  the Great Depression  that little cluster [ __ ] hit the US  markets in the summer of 1929 and  Germany suddenly found that those lovely  American Bankers who'd been giving them  so much money over the previous five  years were no longer picking up the  phone  so to sum it all up by 1930 Germany was  basically broke bereft of allies and  barely the Army to battle a beehive and  yet fewer than 10 years later they would  kick off World War II having somehow  transformed themselves into a world  superpower with the most feared Army in  all of Europe  when you say it like that such a  transformation sounds literally  impossible there simply wasn't enough  time and granted that's completely true  but it turns out the first seeds of  recovery had been planted more than a  decade before the Great Depression even  began  you see ever since the Treaty of  Versailles way back in 1919 Germany had  been secretly rebuilding its military  capabilities  under the Weimar government the German  police force was quietly given training  and Equipment of a distinctly military  nature  Harrow military groups were allowed to  grow unhindered into what soon became  small private armies and money was  discreetly funneled into the research of  forbidden military Technologies  same time state-sponsored clubs started  popping up all over the country publicly  they were perfectly innocent sports  teams youth programs Aviation clubs that  sort of thing but privately they were  little more than military training camps  in which potential leaders were being  picked and future luftwaffe Pilots were  primed  entire generation of Germans was being  readied for war behind closed doors  as per the Treaty of Versailles this was  all totally illegal so these efforts had  to be hidden from the International  Community and that did impose a kind of  natural limit on German rearmament but  the arrival of the Great Depression  dealt fiscal death to Divine our  Republic and it it's safe to say that  the bloke who took their place didn't  overly concern himself with the opinions  of Europe  you might have heard of him actually  he went by Adolf and when he  Consolidated power in Germany in 1933 he  was well and truly tired of the Treaty  of Versailles in fact he planned to tear  that document into neat little squares  so he could wipe his ass with it  during the mid to late 1930s Hitler  kicked off the biggest industrial  expansion in Germany's history as he  Tunes the economy in its entirety  towards a single end War  every man woman and child with a  functional body was put to work for the  greater good many were funneled into  factories producing Munitions and  vehicles of War some furrowed the fields  and others built massive public projects  including the now famous autobahns  Hitler paid for all of this with water  mounted to little more than financial  smoke and mirrors involving shell  companies and Shady promissory notes  known as mifo bills the whole thing was  entirely illegal and hopelessly  unsustainable but Hitler wasn't  interested in Germany's long-term  Financial stability  no  he was going to war and so long as he  won he'd be able to pay off Germany's  mounting debts with all of that loot in  other words he was turning Germany into  the biggest bully in the playground and  he was about to go after the rest of  Europe's lunch money by 1935 Germany's  army had tripled to 300 000 men and its  Air Force something that's very  existence with outlawed boasted 2 500  Cutting Edge warplanes now Hitler wasn't  exactly known for his modesty this is a  man who believed his people were part of  a master race that deserved to rule over  mankind and so he simply couldn't resist  showing off his shiny new Army to the  rest of the world at what he dubbed the  freedom to re-arm Rally  publicly admitting to Breaking the  treaty was a risky move what Hitler had  come up with a Nifty little excuse he  claimed he was re-arming as a purely  defensive measure and not by doing so he  wasn't threatening European peace but  actually helping to maintain it  that might sound ridiculous but what  happened next was downright insane  people actually believed him  looking back with the benefit of  hindsight it's hard to say exactly why  that was perhaps Europe's other  political leaders simply underestimated  just how dangerous Germany was becoming  under Hitler or maybe they were too wary  of rocking the boat for fear of plunging  the world back into war but no Hitler  put on a little [ __ ] military parade  to shout about his giant illegal Army  and the rest of the world simply rolled  over which only served to make the man  with the tiny mustache even bolder by  1939 on the cusp of the biggest war in  history all those years of fevered  preparation had borne lethal and  abundant fruit Hitler's Army contained  more than 4 million soldiers and his  power was absolute  but  alone doesn't entirely explain why  Germany was such a juggernaut in the  first two years of the war Hitler may  have commanded a stronger Army than any  of his enemies in a one-to-one  comparison but World War II wasn't a  singles match it wasn't even a tag team  it was a Royal Rumble involving more  than 50 countries and the combined  forces of the Allies far outnumbered  those of the Axis powers from day one  well actually day two when Hitler fired  the World War II starting pistol by  invading Poland it took Britain and  France two days to decide that might be  a problem and declare war so just 54  hours into a war that would last six  years the Nazis were vastly outnumbered  by the combined forces of the Allies  which also happened to have more money  more resources more ships and planes  more pastries more pretty much  everything and yet we've all read the  history books during the early part of  the war this apparent Underdog tore  through Europe like a Genetically  Enhanced pit bull  in just 19 months Hitler successfully  invaded Poland Denmark Norway Belgium  the Netherlands Luxembourg Franz  Yugoslavia and Greece with the Allies  powerless to stop him  as for how he did it well it turns out  Hitler had a trick up his well-starched  sleeve  [Music]  just 21 years separated the end of the  first world war and the start of the  second but during that time warfare had  changed forever  the trouble was only the Germans had  actually noticed  World War one was fought largely in the  trenches with long periods of stalemate  as huge forces dug in behind fixed lines  attacking such heavily defended  positions was certainly possible but it  cost the aggressor dearly however in  World War version 2.0 fortified trenches  received a huge Nerf thanks to advances  in tanks planes and other newfangled  Weaponry trenches had become defenseless  German tactics heavily hinged on these  hooking machines using their speed to  surprise enemies with a Turret of tanks  and motorized infantry the objective was  today is the enemy and decimates their  defenses this rapid shitstorm on the  ground was simultaneously supported in  the skies by newly designed dive bombers  that focused their efforts where enemy  resistance was strongest whilst also  harassing support lines  you probably know this approach to  murdering the enemy as the famous Nazi  Blitzkrieg tactics a word that literally  translates to lightning War but oddly  enough the term Blitzkrieg was never  actually used by the Germans the term  was picked up by Western media and  somehow stuck anyway in reality and  contrary to popular belief the  foundational principles of Blitzkrieg  strike fast and strike hard with  combined arms weren't anything new the  Germans simply combined classic military  ideas with modern technology in ways  that nobody had ever seen before  the final piece in this devastating  Blitzkrieg puzzle was to Humble radio  much like tanks radios were readily used  in the first world war but they were  large and unreliable and their pitiful  range made them about as viable as  shouting really loudly  but in World War II radios were much  smaller with much better range and so  you don't need to be Sun Tzu to know  that effective communication